{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
You installed playwright: API to automate web browsers.

playwright runs Linux browser binaries under the linuxulator. The host must have
the linux64 kernel module loaded, and the runtime environment must provide:

  - linprocfs on /compat/linux/proc   (browsers resolve themselves via /proc/self/exe)
  - linsysfs  on /compat/linux/sys
  - a writable TMPDIR for the launching user (browser profile + shared memory;
    /tmp is often not writable by a service user)

On a full host:
  sysrc linux_enable=YES && service linux start

In a jail (module loads on the HOST only):
  grant the jail mount rights, e.g. iocage:
    allow_mount=1 allow_mount_linprocfs=1 allow_mount_linsysfs=1 enforce_statfs=1
  then mount linprocfs/linsysfs inside the jail.

Firefox works with the above. Chromium additionally needs fonts: install
linux-rl9-fontconfig and place a font under /compat/linux/usr/share/fonts (e.g.
symlink graphics/dejavu). Chromium is otherwise less reliable on FreeBSD --
Chrome is broken (https://bugs.freebsd.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=289285) and
WebKit is broken due to missing dependencies.

Run 'playwright install' (or 'playwright install firefox') to download browser
binaries before you can use playwright.
EOM
}
